  "slug": "spatial-transcriptomics-6c8f",
  "summary": "Two needle-array methods, LIFE-seq and LANCE-seq, sample spatial RNA from living tissue repeatedly, while FULL-seq pairs chromatin with full-length transcripts.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is extending transcriptomic resolution in time and in transcript structure. LIFE-seq (nanoforest arrays) and LANCE-seq (encoded microneedle arrays) capture spatial RNA from living tissue without terminating it. LIFE-seq follows cortical injury longitudinally within the same mouse. LANCE-seq profiles mouse brain and tracks APAP-induced liver injury over time. FULL-seq jointly profiles chromatin accessibility and full-length transcripts in single cells, linking promoter regulation to alternative first exon usage. On the analysis side, SpaceMACE adds spatial proximity and expression similarity to tumour-cell annotation. PDAC BioPortal integrates bulk, single-nucleus and spatial PDAC cohorts. A TNBC study combines Perturb-seq CRISPRi responses with TF binding priors for interventional network inference, nominating CTCF, MYC and AP-1 members. The remaining studies apply transcriptomic or epigenetic readouts to specific diseases and tissues rather than adding temporal or isoform resolution: KDM3B-ErbB in cholangiocarcinoma, midkine in PDAC, HPV neuroimmune signatures, and healthy cervical snRNA-seq.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
